<article class="env-lemma" id="04S0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04S0">Lemma <span data-tag="04S0">79.15.13</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/04RV" data-tag="04RV">79.15.4</a> assume in addition that $s, t$ are flat and locally of finite presentation and that $U$ is affine. Then there exists an affine scheme $U'$, an étale morphism $U' \to U$, and a point $u' \in U'$ lying over $u$ with $\kappa (u) = \kappa (u')$ such that the restriction $R' = R|_{U'}$ of $R$ to $U'$ is quasi-split over $u'$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The proof of this lemma is literally the same as the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/04RZ" data-tag="04RZ">79.15.11</a> except that “strong splitting” needs to be replaced by “quasi-splitting” (2 times) and that the reference to Lemma <a href="/tag/04RX" data-tag="04RX">79.15.8</a> needs to be replaced by a reference to Lemma <a href="/tag/04RY" data-tag="04RY">79.15.10</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>